      "widgets_values": [
        "## ltx-i2v-shot-lab-example\n\nLTX canvas 1280x704 (width/height must be divisible by 32; 720 and 1080 are invalid).\n\nAfter Queue, click **Save video (MP4) \u2014 open node for preview** for an inline preview. File lands on the host at `${COMFY_OUTPUT_DIR}/ez_*_*.mp4` (container `/outputs`). Save frames PNG is secondary.\n\nUS-safe 5.00s AV I2V print (120 frames @ 24 fps) with last-frame SaveImage.\nModels: ltx-2.5-22b-distilled-transformer-comfy-int8-convrot + gemma4-12b-with-proj-ltx-2.5-comfy-int8-convrot (CLIP ltxv) + ltx-2.5-video-vae-bf16 + ltx-2.5-audio-vae-bf16.\nLTX Community License \u2014 not Apache. $10M company-revenue cap. Disclose AI-generated media; do not strip provenance; do not distill.\n\n90s films: prefer the one-click **film-*-90s-*-lab-example** graphs (Queue once). This graph is the generic 5.00s printer / spark-farm shot. Paste an `ltx_i2v` paragraph from `{film}.shots.yaml` if you iterate a single beat. VHS prefix ez_<slug>_bN_sM_ltx_video. Host stitch: ./scripts/utilities/concat-shots.sh --film go-see --yes\n\nDo not Queue a 90s denoise. US-safe local pack only. No score.\n90s films: prefer the one-click **film-*-90s-*-lab-example** graphs (Queue once). This graph remains the generic 5.00s printer / spark-farm shot.\nPrompt enhance is on by default (on-box Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507). After Queue, the Enhance node shows the prompt CLIP used (or a passthrough reason). Turn Enhance off to use the widget text as-is. Optional style dropdown.\n"
      ],
      "title": "Operator note"
    },
